'The design system ships as a clickable HTML component library, plus Markdown brand guidelines engineers follow when generating pages.':'設計系統直接產出可點擊瀏覽的 HTML 元件庫，並附上 Markdown 品牌規範文件，讓工程師生成頁面時依循。',
'Inconsistent components: built quickly to validate the product, the first version had 3–4 styles for the same component.':'元件樣式不一：初版為了快速上線驗證，同一個元件常常有 3–4 種樣式。',
'Mockups didn’t match the live site: the components in the design files differed a lot from what had actually shipped.':'設計稿和上線網頁落差很大：設計稿裡的元件和實際上線的網頁差很多。',
'Digging through old files: designers had to search many old mockups to decide when to use a component and which style was right.':'做圖要翻大量舊稿：設計團隊每次做圖，都要翻找大量設計稿，才能判斷元件該在什麼時候出現、用哪種樣式。',
'A one-week proposal: a major Japanese hotel group needed a proposal within a week, with no time to draw static mockups from scratch.':'一週內要交出提案：日本大型飯店集團的提案時程很緊，沒有時間從零畫靜態稿。',
'Start from what actually shipped':'以實際上線的樣子為準',
'Mockups alone would miss styles that only existed in production. I had AI write a crawler that recorded the component styles on the live site. Once Claude gained Playwright, I had it open the real pages and inspect them directly.':'只看設計稿會漏掉只存在於正式環境的樣式。我請 AI 寫爬蟲，爬取上線網站的元件樣式並記錄下來；後來 Claude 有了 Playwright，就直接讓它開瀏覽器檢查實際頁面。',
'Bring the live site back into Figma':'把上線網頁轉回 Figma',
'I built a plugin that turns live web components into Figma files, so the design files finally matched what users actually see.':'我做了一個插件，把上線網頁的元件轉成 Figma 檔，讓設計稿和使用者實際看到的版本對齊。',
'A full inventory':'全面盤點',
'The audit covered everything from basic components to dialogs, dropdowns and date and location pickers, up to the layout rules for whole pages.':'範圍從基礎元件，到彈窗、下拉選單、時間與地點選擇器等組件，再到整體頁面的 layout 規範。',
'Scenario first, then style':'先定義情境，再決定樣式',
'For each component I defined which situation it belongs to, how users behave there, and which style follows. Designers no longer have to dig through old files for the answer, and the 3–4 variants became one.':'每個元件都明確定義在什麼操作情境下，使用者會有什麼行為，對應什麼樣式。設計時不用再翻舊稿找答案，原本的 3–4 種樣式也統整成一種。',
'Tokens and a clickable component library':'Token 與可點擊的元件庫',
'I used Figma MCP to read component values and had Claude Code convert them into design tokens, then generate the component library from the token structure as a clickable HTML page.':'用 Figma MCP 讀取元件數值，請 Claude Code 轉成 design token，再依 token 結構產出元件庫，整理成可點擊瀏覽的 HTML 元件庫頁面。',
'Brand guidelines for engineers':'給工程師的品牌規範文件',
'I also wrote a set of Markdown guidelines, so engineers follow the company’s brand rules when they generate early pages.':'我另外產出一系列 Markdown 規範文件，讓工程師在初期生成頁面時，也能依照公司的品牌規範。',
'The client':'客戶規模',
'The client was the hotel business of a Japanese listed financial group, running more than ten hotels and hot-spring ryokan across Japan with about 3,500 rooms, and a key account for the company.':'客戶是日本上市金融集團旗下的飯店事業，在全日本經營十多間飯店與溫泉旅館、約 3,500 間客房，也是公司的重要客戶。',
'A working prototype in one week':'一週內交出可操作的原型',
'Within a week, I explored ideas, aligned with the team, and assembled a working web prototype from the component library.':'一週內完成發想、和團隊內部討論出共識，再用元件庫組出可實際操作的網頁原型。',
'Built for clients and sales':'客戶與業務都能直接使用',
'The client could try it on their own computer, and sales could present straight from it instead of static screenshots. We won the account.':'客戶可以在自己的電腦上實際操作；業務也能直接用這個網頁簡報，不再只靠靜態截圖說明。最後順利簽下這個客戶。',
'A design system has to stay in sync with what is live. When the product departs from the spec, I record the exception as a reference for the next change, rather than letting the two drift apart. It also means checking that every component behaves the same way across the product, not just that it looks the same.':'設計系統要能跟線上狀態保持同步。當實際產品和規範出現例外時，要記錄下來作為下次改動的參考，而不是讓兩者各自走偏；同時也要思考每個組件的互動行為是否一致，而不只是外觀一致。',
